title:: BMSoundFilePlayer
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - a sound file player
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMSoundFilePlayer is a soundfile player with integration in the BEASTmulch library. It provides standard functionality, i.e. play, pause, stop, change rate, etc.

Instances can serve as Time References, and will update any dependants with strong::update(\time, timeInSeconds, rateOfChange, referenceTime):: messages. (See class link::Classes/Object:: for a discussion of dependancy mechanisms.) It also updates dependants with the following messages:

code::\loading:: - when loading of a file begins
code::\loaded:: - when a sound file has been loaded
code::\base:: - when its time base has changed (i.e. a file has been loaded or buffer cleared)
code::\play:: - when playback begins or resumes
code::\playFailed:: - if playback failed
code::\stop:: - when playback stopped
code::\pause:: - when playback pauses
code::\bufferFreed:: - when its buffer is freed

See also: link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractAudioSource::, link::Classes/Other/BMSoundFilePlayerGUI::, link::Overview/Time References and Automation::

Section:: File Size Limits

In the current implementation BMSoundFilePlayer loads files into memory rather than streaming from disk. This avoids potential dropout, etc. resulting from disk access, but places some practical upper limits on file size.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new BMSoundFilePlayer.

argument:: maxNumChannels
The maximum number of output channels for this player. Default value is 2.
argument:: target
Target for this object's link::Classes/Group::. If target is not a Group or link::Classes/Synth::, it will be converted as follows: If it is a link::Classes/Server::, it will be converted to the default_group of that server. If it is nil, to the default group of the default Server. strong::Note::: A Synth is not a valid target for code::\addToHead:: and code::\addToTail::.
argument:: addAction
one of the following Symbols:		
code::\addToHead:: - (the default) add at the head of the group specified by target
code::\addToTail:: - add at the tail of the group specified by target
code::\addAfter:: - add immediately after target in its server's node order
code::\addBefore:: - add immediately before target in its server's node order
code::\addReplace:: - replace target and take its place in its server's node order
argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the name of this object. If not supplied one will be generated.


INSTANCEMETHODS::
	
method:: sampleDur
Returns the sample duration based on the currently loaded buffer's sample rate.
				
method:: buffer
Get the currently loaded link::Classes/Buffer::.
				
method:: rate
Set or get the current playback rate. 1 is normal, -1 is backwards, 2 is twice as fast, etc.
				
method:: loading
Returns a link::Classes/Boolean:: indicating if a file load is in progress.
				
method:: synth
If playing, return this object's playback link::Classes/Synth::, nil otherwise.
				
method:: bus
Set or get this object's output audio Bus. This should match strong::maxNumChannels:: in size. 
				

method:: read
Read a sound file into memory.
		
argument:: path
A link::Classes/String:: indicating the path of the file to be loaded.
argument:: action
An optional link::Classes/Function:: to be evaluated when loading is complete. It will be passed the receiver as an argument.

code::		
p = BMSoundFilePlayer(name:\foo);
p.read("sounds/a11wlk01.wav", {|pl| "% read successfully\n".postf(pl.name)}); 
p.free; // cleanup
::


method:: play
Play the currently loaded file. If playing is already underway this is ignored. At the end of the file playback will stop automatically.

argument::startTime
Offset in seconds into the file at which to start playback.
argument:: out
An optional link::Classes/Integer:: or link::Classes/Bus:: to use for output. If nil (the default) the object's internal (private) bus is used.
		
code::
p = BMSoundFilePlayer(name:\foo);
p.read("sounds/a11wlk01.wav");
p.play(0, 0); // play from start out bus 0;
p.play(1, 0); // skip ahead
p.play(0, 0).rate_(0.5); // half speed
p.free;
::


method:: stop
If currently playing stop, otherwise ignore.


method:: togglePlay
If currently playing, pause playback. If stopped or paused, start or resume playback.


method:: pause
If currently playing pause playback.


method:: freeBuffer
Free the currently loaded Buffer.
		
		
method:: free
Free this object's resources and nodes. After calling this it should not be used.


method:: setTime
If currently playing jump to the new time, if not start playback at strong::time:: in a paused (i.e. cued) state.

argument:: time
The new time in seconds.


method:: asBMInOutArray
Returns this object's outputs as a link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::.
		
code::
p = BMSoundFilePlayer(name:\foo);
p.asBMInOutArray; // foo-1 etc.
p.free;
::


method:: path
Returns a String indicating the path of the currently loaded sound file.
	
		
method:: duration
Returns the duration in seconds of the currently loaded sound file, or nil if one is not loaded.


method:: gui
Creates and returns a link::Classes/Other/BMSoundFilePlayerGUI:: with this object as an argument.
		
code::
p = BMSoundFilePlayer(name:\foo);
p.bus = 0; // for the sake of example
p.gui.onClose_({p.free});
::


Examples::

code::
// example with a matrix for routing
s.boot;

p = BMSoundFilePlayer(name:\foo);
p.read("sounds/a11wlk01.wav"); // mono, so only out foo-1

// make a speaker list
(
l = [[-30, 'L'], [30, 'R'], [0, 'C'], [-110, 'Ls'], [110, 'Rs']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
)

// make a matrix for connections
m = BMAudioMatrix(p, l, name:'Router');

m.connect('foo-1', 'L');

m.gui; p.gui; // play with the GUIs
p.free;
::
